cdp-fx — passthrough placeholder WCLAP module for an offline CDP effect stage.

This module is original code, MIT (see LICENSE); it links nothing of the
Composer's Desktop Project. The CDP programs it points at are rendered by the
vendored cdp-wasm 0.7.0 package in ../cdp-engine/third_party/cdp-wasm (MIT AND
LGPL-2.1-or-later) — see ../cdp-engine/NOTICE. The effect catalog it indexes
(param 0) is ../cdp-engine/catalog.json, generated from that package.

Why a passthrough: CDP effects are offline (file -> file) programs and cannot run
in a realtime CLAP process(). In our wclap-rack hosts the effect is applied by
the page-side wclap.cdp/1 bridge (reference-host/cdp-bridge.mjs, CDPBridge
fxChain) between the cdp-engine's per-note generator render and the delivery,
using THIS device's params from the rack document; at extract/QD time the same
chain runs over full rendered audio (CDPBridge.applyEffectToWav). In any other
host (DAW, test host without the bridge) this device is a bit-transparent
stereo passthrough.
